              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for to increase, then the Marathi for to reduce."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: चुकणे",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चुकणे — cukṇe — \"to miss; to go wrong\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चुकणे (cukṇe) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from cukk, \"fall short of, stop\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 4848). CDIAL says Prakrit cukka, \"fallen, mistaken\", took the place of Sanskrit cyuta, \"fallen\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
